{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Doctor, he's in the room. I did the observations: blood pressure is one thirty-eight over eighty-four, pulse seventy-six, oxygen ninety-eight percent, and the temperature thirty-six point six.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand, thanks. Sit yourself down there. What has you in?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Stomach. Sleep.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): The stomach first. Is it a pain?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Pain.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Where are you pointing?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Middle.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Up high, in under the breastbone?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long has it been at you?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Two weeks. No. Three.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Three weeks. Is it there all the time, or coming and going?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Coming and going.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Worse after your food?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any burning up into the chest?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting with it?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Black stools, or blood when you go?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): And the sleep. What way is it off?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Waking.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Waking at night. Any idea how long that's been going on?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): No date on the sleep, that's fine. I'll book an ultrasound of the tummy for this week. Before I send that off, are you on any tablets yourself?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Anything in the press at home that isn't yours, so I don't put it on your chart by mistake?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Mam's metformin.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Your mam's metformin. That's hers, not yours, so it stays off your list. Any allergy to a medicine?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): And do you take a drink?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Socially.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Socially can mean all sorts. What would a normal week actually look like?",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (PATIENT): Bottle of wine. Most nights. Perhaps.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm not giving out. A bottle most nights is a different picture for the stomach and the liver, so that plan may need to change. I'll have a feel of the tummy first.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): Tummy's soft, tender across the upper middle, no guarding and no lump. Any shortness of breath, or a cough?",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, I'll think it through out loud. Tender up top, pain after food for three weeks, heartburn now and again, broken sleep, and the wine. I'd say it's acid, a gastritis. I wouldn't rule out the drink irritating the lining.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm changing that ultrasound. We won't book the scan now. I'll order liver blood tests today, because of the wine. We might do a scan if the pain has not settled in a fortnight.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): For a stomach tablet I'll start you on lansoprazole, twenty milligrams... no, omeprazole, forty milligrams, once every morning, by mouth.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ease off the wine if you can, even a few nights with none. There's no lecture in it. I'll see you back in a fortnight.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (NURSE): I'll leave the liver blood form at the desk, so he can have them taken on the way out."
 ],
